    <!-- Help & FAQ Screen -->
    <string name="faq_title">Frequently Asked Questions</string>

    <string name="faq_q1">Why do exam portals reject photos larger than 50 KB?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Most Indian government exam servers (like SSC, IBPS, UPSC, Railway) set strict file size limits between 20 KB and 50 KB. If a file is even 50.1 KB, the upload server rejects it. FormPic guarantees your final file size stays strictly below the selected limit.</string>

    <string name="faq_q2">Does FormPic upload my personal photos to the internet?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">No. 100% of face detection, background isolation, cropping, and compression runs on your device using on-device ML Kit models. Your personal photos never leave your phone.</string>

    <string name="faq_q3">How do I get the cleanest white background?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">Stand in front of a plain wall with uniform lighting on your face. Avoid harsh backlighting or deep shadows behind your head. If any edge needs fine-tuning, use our built-in Touch Up brush.</string>

    <string name="faq_q4">Where is the downloaded photo saved?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">The photo is saved directly into your device Gallery / Photos under the "Pictures/FormPic" folder, ready to be attached to any online form.</string>

    <string name="faq_q5">Why does a 25 KB or 50 KB photo look slightly softer?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">25 KB is an extremely small digital file. FormPic uses an intelligent binary-search algorithm to pack maximum possible detail and clarity into the tiny size allowed by government portals.</string>

    <string name="faq_q6">Why was an advertisement displayed before download?</string>
    <string name="faq_a6">FormPic is 100% free with no watermark. A single polite ad supports our ongoing development and serverless on-device model updates. If an ad fails or you are offline, your download will still proceed immediately.</string>
